<header><p class="st-kicker">protectorate · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">North-Western Rhodesia</h1><p class="st-meta">1899 CE – 1911 CE · capital Kalomo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The British South Africa Company territory west of the Kafue, built on treaties with the Lozi king Lewanika.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lozi-people">Lozi</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lewanika">Lewanika</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/barotseland">Barotseland</a>, seeking protection against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndebele-kingdom">Ndebele</a> and Portuguese, signed concessions with agents of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-south-africa-company">British South Africa Company</a> in 1890 and later. In 1899 an Order in Council created Barotziland-North-Western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rhodesia">Rhodesia</a> under company administration, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalomo">Kalomo</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The administrator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-coryndon">Robert Coryndon</a> and his successors ruled through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lewanika">Lewanika</a>, who kept considerable authority in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lozi-people">Barotse</a> heartland. The railway from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulawayo">Bulawayo</a> crossed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-victoria">Victoria</a> Falls bridge in 1905 and reached the Broken Hill mine in 1906. The capital moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livingstone-zambia">Livingstone</a> in 1907. Hut tax pushed men to work in Southern Rhodesian mines.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1911 North-Western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rhodesia">Rhodesia</a> was merged with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/north-eastern-rhodesia">North-Eastern Rhodesia</a> to form <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/northern-rhodesia">Northern Rhodesia</a>, still under company rule, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livingstone-zambia">Livingstone</a> as capital. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/barotseland">Barotseland</a> kept a special status that continued into independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/north-western-rhodesia.jpg" alt="North-Western Rhodesia" width="320" height="162"><figcaption>Image: Mangwanani · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_British_South_Africa_Company.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1899 CE – 1911 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>protectorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kalomo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Lewanika, Robert Coryndon</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional religion, Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Silozi, English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/zambia">Zambia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Barotziland-North-Western Rhodesia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1905&amp;focus=north-western-rhodesia" aria-label="North-Western Rhodesia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5400 2810 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where North-Western Rhodesia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5720 3066L5629 3000M5720 3066L5842 3096M5720 3066L5752 2973"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5629 3000h0M5842 3096h0M5752 2973h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5720 3066h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5720 3066h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kalomo. <a href="/atlas?year=1905&amp;focus=north-western-rhodesia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
